{"availability":"available","full":"maddisondesigns/customizer-custom-controls","name":"customizer-custom-controls","description":"WordPress Customizer Custom Controls","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":409,"forks":115,"created":"2017-05-04T14:40:11Z","updated":"2026-05-20T03:31:08Z","branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":["customizer","jquery","php","wordpress","wordpress-customizer"],"demo":"https://www.tinymce.com/docs/demo/basic-example/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T14:33:25.567Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T14:33:25.567Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T14:33:25.567Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T14:33:25.567Z","stars":409,"forks":115}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Author: Anthony Hortin Author URI: License: GNU General Public License v2 or later License URI: Version: 1.3.3","There are several different types of basic Core Controls built into the Customizer that are ready to use straight-out-of-the-box. These include text, checkbox, textarea, radio, select and dropdown-pages controls. Later versions of WordPress also introduced Color, Media, Image and Cropped Image controls. If none of the basic core controls suit your needs, you can create and add your own custom controls.","This example code shows how to incorporate Customizer functionality into your theme (or plugin), including examples of how to create Panels, Sections and how to update the Live Preview window. As well as showing the usage of the (built-in) core controls, there are also a number of Custom Controls that have been built that you're welcome to make use of."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/maddisondesigns/customizer-custom-controls/blob/master/readme.md","fingerprint":"4597af9109908bb00988ec440a8b84f2a0717bd3fc820f6158707421138ebb2e","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T07:02:03.480Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T14:16:56.503Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Author: Ant